. Configure Caching and Load Modules
This sets your Hugging Face cache location to your scratch space so you don't run out of storage, and loads the required system modules:   
PDF

Bash
echo "export HF_HOME=/scratch/pgopalan/cache/hf_cache" >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc

ml load gnul2/12.3.0
ml load python/3.11.7-cx
ml load cuda/12.4.0
ml load git
2. Create the Project Structure
Navigate to your specific scratch space and create the necessary folder structure:   
PDF

Bash
cd /scratch/pgopalan/
mkdir langsense
cd langsense
mkdir models datasets logs src
mkdir logs/data_processing logs/slurm_logs logs/checkpoints logs/configs logs/slurm_scripts
3. Create and Activate the Virtual Environment
Create your isolated Python environment:   
PDF

Bash
python -m venv nanotron-env
source nanotron-env/bin/activate
pip install --upgrade pip
4. Install Dependencies
Install PyTorch, clone the Nanotron repository, and install the required Python packages:   
PDF

Bash
pip install torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu124

git clone https://github.com/iamshnoo/nanotron.git
cd nanotron
pip install -e .

pip install datasets==3.6.0 transformers numba wandb ninja triton datatrove==0.3.0 psutil pybind11
Download and install the specific Flash Attention wheel:   
PDF

Bash
wget https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/releases/download/v2.7.3/flash_attn-2.7.3+cu12torch2.6cxx11abiFALSE-cp311-cp311-linux_x86_64.whl
pip install flash_attn-2.7.3+cu12torch2.6cxx11abiFALSE-cp311-cp311-linux_x86_64.whl
(Note: Correcting the typo at the end of the document's installation list, you should run this to get the standard fine-tuning libraries):   
PDF

Bash
pip install accelerate bitsandbytes peft liger-kernel
5. Authenticate Services
Log in to Hugging Face and Weights & Biases:   
PDF

Bash
huggingface-cli login
wandb login
